# Line endings, decided once, for everyone.
#
# Before this file existed the repository held 94 CRLF files and 34 LF ones with
# nothing enforcing either, because it was written on Windows and has never had
# a second contributor. The first Linux contributor whose editor normalises a
# file on save would have opened a pull request touching every line of it, and
# nobody could have reviewed that.
#
# It has already cost this project once: bundled skills are parsed by a
# front-matter regex anchored on "\n" (Claudpress_Skills::parse_markdown, in
# includes/class-skills.php), and a CRLF skill file simply did not match. There
# is a str_replace() normalising newlines in front of that regex now. This file
# is the fix one level up.

# Baseline: normalise every text file to LF inside the repository. Git decides
# what is text; anything it decides is binary is left alone.
* text=auto

# --- Files that must be LF to work, not merely to be tidy -------------------

# Shebang scripts. A CRLF shell script fails with "bad interpreter: no such
# file or directory", which is one of the least helpful error messages in
# computing. bin/build-zip.sh is CRLF in the index today.
*.sh    text eol=lf

# GitHub Actions workflows and issue forms are parsed on GitHub's Linux runners.
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf

# bin/build-zip.sh assembles the release zip by copying files straight out of
# the working tree, so whatever line endings are checked out here are the ones
# every user installs — on a Linux host, from a Windows checkout. Everything
# that goes into that zip is therefore pinned to LF rather than left to the
# platform.
*.php   text eol=lf
*.txt   text eol=lf

# Skills are shipped in that zip, parsed by the front-matter regex above, and
# signed byte-for-byte for the release feed. Two contributors on two platforms
# must produce identical bytes or the signature is meaningless.
skills/*.md text eol=lf

# Node and JSON tooling. Not strictly required, but there is no reason for the
# test runner's files to differ by platform.
*.mjs   text eol=lf
*.js    text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf

# --- Binary: never diff, never munge line endings ---------------------------
# Listed ahead of need. Screenshots for the plugin listing and demo video
# captures are coming, and the moment one lands without a rule here Git may
# guess wrong and corrupt it on checkout.

*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.webp  binary
*.ico   binary
*.zip   binary
*.mp4   binary
*.mov   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary

# --- Diff quality -----------------------------------------------------------
# Puts the enclosing function or class in the @@ hunk header, which is the
# difference between reviewing a diff and hunting for where you are in it.
*.php   diff=php
*.md    diff=markdown
